    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d336">

                <pb facs="0499" n="483" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg483"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811F.812/3–348</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of the Army</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Royall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-03-03">March 3, 1948</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Secretary</hi>: I am enclosing for your
                    information a copy of a letter of this date which I have addressed to The
                    President, submitting my observations on various interoceanic canal routes and
                    alternative methods of transit, made during my trip of inspection in Mexico and
                    Central America in February 1948.</p>
                <p>I shall be pleased to communicate further with you when I have received from the
                    Governor of the Panama Canal his report on the additional investigations in the
                    Republic of Colombia which are discussed in my letter to The President.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kenneth</hi> C. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Royall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d336-a1.xml" xpointer="d336-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
